[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2742848765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104423#issuecomment-2742848765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104423","id":2742848765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jfIz9","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-21T09:47:18Z","updated_at":"2025-03-21T09:47:18Z","body":"Physics interpolation is not specific to physics objects (despite the confusing name), it's named this way because it interpolates visual elements between physics ticks / fixed framerate.\n\nCC @lawnjelly @rburing ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2742848765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745036819","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104423#issuecomment-2745036819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104423","id":2745036819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jnfAT","user":{"login":"Xorblax","id":98433469,"node_id":"U_kgDOBd35vQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98433469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax","html_url":"https://github.com/Xorblax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-22T05:49:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-22T05:49:16Z","body":"I see, in that case the tooltip for the toggle should be updated as it says it interpolates the transforms of specifically physics objects. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745036819/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746101256","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104423#issuecomment-2746101256","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104423","id":2746101256,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jri4I","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T09:03:29Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T09:35:26Z","body":"Akien covers it mostly above, physics interpolation applies to all nodes, and the name is confusing (I would have preferred it to be called FTI (\"fixed timestep interpolation\") from the get go).\n\nAdditionally it may not have been emphasized enough in the release notes (I don't generally get too involved with 4.x), but physics interpolation is both:\n* Experimental at this stage, and subject to change (and indeed 3D is likely going to be changed significantly soon with #104269 ). Consider it a \"work in progress\" as we are reliant on feedback from 4.4 to make changes / fix bugs.\n* Not all nodes are guaranteed to work with it, especially GPUParticles in 2D and 3D, if these work at all currently it is more \"by accident\". CPUParticles are currently more reliable (as they have changes made specifically to support FTI), but I can only speak for the situation in 3.x, as @rburing did the conversion for 4.x, and particles may work slightly differently.\n\nAfter #104269, for `GPUParticles3D` in your MRP rather than turn off physics interpolation for the whole project, you can turn it off just for the GPUParticles node via `physics_interpolation_mode` (either in script or in the inspector for the node).\n\nParticles in particular often need special treatment because they were (at least in 3.x) defined in an awkward coordinate space for global particles, which doesn't gel well with interpolation, and this needs to be fixed first before they can be interpolated.\n\n> I see, in that case the tooltip for the toggle should be updated as it says it interpolates the transforms of specifically physics objects.\n\nTo clarify, which tooltip is this, and what wording in particular is causing confusion?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746101256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746340833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104423#issuecomment-2746340833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104423","id":2746340833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jsdXh","user":{"login":"Xorblax","id":98433469,"node_id":"U_kgDOBd35vQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98433469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax","html_url":"https://github.com/Xorblax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xorblax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T17:59:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T17:59:30Z","body":"In Project Settings/General/Physics/Common there's the toggle for Physics Interpolation, where the tooltip that appears on mousing over it says: \"If true, the renderer will interpolate the transforms of physics objects between the last two transforms, so that smooth motion is seen even when physics ticks do not coincide with rendered frames.\"\nThis does not seem to at all suggest that the interpolation applies to non-physics objects, hence my confusion.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746340833/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746349377","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104423#issuecomment-2746349377","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104423","id":2746349377,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jsfdB","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T18:14:55Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T18:14:55Z","body":"> This does not seem to at all suggest that the interpolation applies to non-physics objects, hence my confusion.\n\nAh you are absolutely right, this is incorrect, it was introduced in my original PR #52846 (it may have been in response to a request for change by a reviewer), I'll do a PR to fix this tooltip. 👍 ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746349377/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]